## 🧰 Hardware & Components

### 1. Main Electronics

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| Arduino UNO | 1× | Main controller |
| MAX7219 8×8 Dot Matrix Module | 4× | 2×2 LED matrix game display |
| OLED Display 0.96" (SSD1306, I²C) | 1× | Menu, scores, and status information |
| Joystick Module (XY + SW) | 1× | Game control |
| Tactile Push Button | 3× | OK/Select, LEFT, and RIGHT controls |

### 2. Power Supply

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| 5V 2A DC Adapter | 1× | Main external power supply |
| DC Barrel Jack Connector / Breadboard Power Module | 1× | Connects the external power adapter to the system |

### 3. Wiring & Interconnection

| Component | Quantity | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| Male-to-Male Jumper Wires | As required | Breadboard connections |
| Male-to-Female Jumper Wires | As required | Module-to-board connections |
| Female-to-Female Jumper Wires | As required | Module interconnections |
| Breadboard | 1× | Prototyping and temporary wiring |
| PCB Stripboard / Perfboard | Optional | Permanent installation |

### 4. Wire Color Convention

| Color | Signal |
|---|---|
| 🔴 Red | VCC / 5V |
| ⚫ Black | GND / Common Ground |
| 🟡 Yellow | Data signals — DIN, SDA, VRx, Button signals |
| 🟢 Green | CS / VRy |
| 🔵 Blue | CLK / SCL / SW |
| 🟣 Purple / 🟠 Orange / 🌸 Pink | MAX7219 Daisy Chain — DOUT → DIN |

> **Note:** Wire colors are used as a visual convention to make the wiring easier to understand and troubleshoot. The actual electrical function depends on the connected pin, not the wire color.
